## Multi-Agent Development (Git Worktrees)

Use worktrees **only** when multiple agents need to work in parallel:

```bash
# Create worktree for parallel work
git worktree add ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2 [branch]

# Work in the worktree
cd ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2

# When done, remove worktree
git worktree remove ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2
```

**Key principle**: Worktrees are for parallel work, NOT branching strategy.

See [`DEVELOPMENT.md`](./DEVELOPMENT.md) for complete worktree commands and workflow tier details.

